From bc34a18a4a0acb4343f2428f917bb3f45e3dafff Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Hades <15710513+hadesdevls@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 11 Nov 2026 06:11:58 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] xbmc, tools/dvbridge: format the lines added since the Kodi
 base to the 100 columns of .clang-format

git clang-format (clang-format 21 from Ubuntu's archive, Kodi's .clang-format) over the lines
that Hades added to xbmc/ since the base, now that all of it is on one tree; and
the comment lines of the added lines that are over 100 columns (ReflowComments is off), in xbmc/
and in tools/dvbridge, wrapped with a script that checks that the code with its comments blanked
out is the same before and after. Three trailing comments of xbmc/ went to their own line.

Only layout changes: the tokens of every file are the same before and after (apart from long
string literals that clang-format splits into adjacent literals, which the compiler joins) and so
is the set of #include lines, which clang-format sorts inside their blocks. Code lines of
tools/dvbridge over 100 columns (GLSL in string macros, long calls, in the C style of that folder,
which has over a thousand of them already) are left as they are.
